  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'the downmapper allows you to automatically create lower difficulties based
    on a higher one.

    every section has an enable toggle. if a section is disabled,
    the downmapper will not alter the mapping with those instructions.

    some
    values are labled as lead-in time. lead in time means how many ticks have to
    be empty space before such a target can appear.

    the same goes for pause
    after - how much time in ticks has to be empty after such a target appeared.


    custom
    values are saved and loaded per difficulty.


    in the doubles section, there
    is a prioritize hitsounds over beat toggle. it applies to everything, not just
    doubles. if the downmapper has to remove a target, e.g. to ensure lead-in time,
    the downmapper will prioritize the target with the stronger hitsound. hitsound
    strength is as follows, from strongest to weakest: percussion > snare > kick
    > chain start > chain node > melee > silent

    only use this option if you
    have properly authored hitsounds!


    <b>streams</b>

    streams are standard
    notes appearing in quick succesion. something is considered a stream after more
    than thatmax consecutive targets appeared in intervals that are as fast or faster
    than the max stream speed (in ticks). if fast streams 2 chains is ticked, it
    will convert found streams into chains.


    <b>chains</b>

    chains have
    a pause after setting for same and other hand.

    checking remove targets during
    chains will remove all other targets that appear while a chain is active.

    convert
    chains to targets deletes the chain and replaces the chain start with a normal
    target.


    <b>doubles</b>

    un-cross all doubles will make sure that the
    right hand target is always right, and left hand target always left. '
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8d6ffc87ae696bb49b961911c4703d7d, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2143181537736950723, guid: 8d6ffc87ae696bb49b961911c4703d7d,
